<title>JAPAN: MOF did not discuss Thai baht with Japan PM--Jiji.</title>
<headline>MOF did not discuss Thai baht with Japan PM--Jiji.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eisuke Sakakibara, an influential official at Japan's Ministry of Finance, was quoted on Thursday by Jiji news service as saying that he did not discuss the Thai baht in a meeting with Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto.  </p>
<p>Asked whether he spoke about the baht with Hashimoto, Sakakibara was quoted as saying: &quot;The issue was not brought up.&quot;</p>
<p>Sakakibara, speaking to reporters at the Prime Minister's Office, also said that there was no change in Japan's foreign exchange policies and that Japan will not use exchange rates as an instrument of trade policy, Jiji reported.</p>
</text>
